{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1518782-should-we-be-playing-with-the-anishinaabe","id":1518782,"title":"Should we be playing with the Anishinaabe?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-07-25T15:12:41-07:00","id":1518782,"title":"Should we be playing with the Anishinaabe?","content":"I just ran into a post on Tumblr where the OP was asserting that Anishinaabe folklore (and specificically the w*ndigo) were a Closed culture, not meant to be shared with outsiders, and so using it in fiction was racist appropriation. They were specifically making a point involving Yellowjackets and Hannibal and deer-head imagery (which yes, I'm aware is an appropriative later addition), but they seemed to believe that this was a general rule.<br /> <br /> Does anyone know the &quot;official&quot; or dominant Anishinaabe stance on using their folklore? Since I run a Scion game set in Philadelphia, the Anishinaabe are one of the main folklores that inform the Legendary background of the setting. I was under the impression that this was okay, if used with respect, since they made it into the book and other Native cultures didn't because of this very issue, but now I'm unsure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24028-mike-mccall","name":"Mike McCall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24028_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"55"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-26T10:31:01-07:00","id":1518830,"title":"","content":"Basil Johnston, an Anishinaabe storyteller, published several books on traditional Anishinaabe beliefs and ceremonies. The one most relevant to a Scion game is <i>The Manitous: The Supernatural World of the Ojibway</i>. His purpose was to share this knowledge with people outside the Anishinaabe community. So at least one important Anishinaabe elder felt it was appropriate to share this sort of thing widely.<br /> <br /> Additionally, for living traditions and especially those of indigenous peoples, Onyx Path seeks to work with members of those communities in writing up the pantheons. They had said they won't ever be doing the Hopi or Navajo pantheons because members of those communities made it clear that they don't want their traditional beliefs shared.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26114-muskrat","name":"Muskrat","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"75"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-28T20:27:34-07:00","id":1519069,"title":"","content":"Thanks, Muskrat. I know Onyx Path's general policies, which is why I was confused when this person was asserting something different. It's good to have a counter-example. For now I will tread carefully, but assume that I am on okay ground using the Lenape people (who aren't actually Anishinaabe, but the Manitou apply anyway given how Scion does things) in my Philly game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24028-mike-mccall","name":"Mike McCall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24028_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"55"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-29T05:31:38-07:00","id":1519105,"title":"","content":"I try to quietly step when playing with First Nations beliefs as it can be sensitive and varied. As the Ponca head office is up the street from me, I can ask questions and if they don't want me to use something, I consider that only fair. That said, I've found a lot that doesn't square with what is often taught in Schools or University (no surprise there), and I tend to highlight the good and bad in all groups. So the players can make their own decisions and feel I'm not trying to favor any particular group. I create stories, not lectures.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13091-thewanderingjewels","name":"TheWanderingJewels","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13091_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-19T02:39:09-07:00","id":1522783,"title":"","content":"I just posted a pantheon I made based on my own tribe (Tsalagi, aka Cherokee). Most other Natives I know would be fine with other people using their mythology/religion in this way. The thing many of us fear is having all of this knowledge die out, so anything that preserves it is often seen as a good thing. The main thing is to be respectful and not mock their beliefs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28198-ahisgewaya","name":"Ahisgewaya","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28198_2.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-20T10:15:41-07:00","id":1522830,"title":"","content":"It depends a lot on which tribe and person you ask. with the Manitou, well... the one who complains is from Tumblr, the pantheon has been on the set for years and is based on the book by an Ashininaabe person, there is no fault.<br /> It's a shame the Hopi also refused, I hope the Sioux, Inuit and Iroquois have a different opinion. (The Orenda must expand!)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28200,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28200-plebsparks","user":"PlebSparks","date":". 11-29-2023, 01:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28200-plebsparks","name":"PlebSparks","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28200_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-08T15:41:37-07:00","id":1541753,"title":"","content":"I just finished a story arc in my Scion campaign that was set among the Ashininaabe people and pantheon presented in the corebook. I did a lot of research ahead of time to learn as much as I could. We had lots of discussions within our player group on how to be respectful and how things were to be played out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:georgia\">Organizer for the Dead Gamers Society: The So Cal World of Darkness Meetup. </span><a href=\"http://www.meetup.com/Dead-Gamers-Society/\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.meetup.com/Dead-Gamers-Society/</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/85-drumheller","name":"Drumheller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar85_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"55"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}